WEBVTT

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.230
Aren't the flowers pretty, Rin?

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.390
Monet, I brought cake.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.260
What's wrong?

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.400
Nothing.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.700
I was going to throw it away anyway.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.120
It's fine.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:20.140
<b>Magic-Kyun Renaissance</b>

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Blown by a Mischievous Wind

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.980
This must be a May storm.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.140
A May storm? As in the month of May?

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:49.770
Yeah. Apparently it's the 
perfect day for goodbyes.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.260
This wind would help you get over anything.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.130
It does seem that way.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.650
Wh-What is this?

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.490
How pretty. It's like stained glass.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.200
What a cute drawing.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:07.590
Yeah.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.460
Practice for the Art Session?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:22.090
<b>63 days until the Summer Festival!</b>

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.330
Yes. There are two months left 
until the Hoshi Festival.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.980
I thought we could start practicing

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.300
collaborations of our magical arts 
with those of us who are here.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:23.700
Very well.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.100
Then I'll tell you the 
secret of the Art Session.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:29.880
Secret?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.310
Make Your Hearts One

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.310
"Make your hearts one"?

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:37.320
That's right.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:42.360
The magical arts you specialize 
in are all different genres.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.640
If you want to collaborate,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.500
you'll first have to 
synchronize your breathing.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.620
Synchronize...

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.280
...our breathing?

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.130
What does that mean?

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.250
Yes, sir! I don't really get it, 
but I hear you loud and clear!

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.510
<i>You understand him?</i>

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.880
If we need to synchronize our breathing, 
there's only one thing to do!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.220
Your breathing is out of sync, Aigasaki.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.180
Sorry!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.770
Don't worry about it.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.620
Next, we'll try this!

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.270
Ready, and...

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.760
Why are we swinging slippers?

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.030
You really feel it in your arms, don't you?

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.680
Your breathing is out of sync, Aigasaki!

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.200
Sorry.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.790
Don't worry about it.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.310
What are they doing?

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.300
Next, we'll try this!

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.200
Bamboo shoot squats.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.760
Is this really going to unify our hearts?

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.240
Your breathing is out of sync, Aigasaki.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.160
Sorry.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.020
Don't worry about it.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.150
This is what we should be doing.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.110
Volleyball?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.870
I've never played sexy volleyball before.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.160
I don't care what kind 
of volleyball you play.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.780
We're going to pass the 
ball ten thousand times.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.370
Ten thousand?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:15.000
Yes. All of us will synchronize our breathing
 and pass the ball ten thousand times.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.540
All right! This will really 
bring our hearts together!

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.750
Great idea. I feel really 
excited about this one.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.400
Here we go.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.010
Yeah!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.380
Here I go.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.030
This is going to take a while.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.700
Shall we go?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.270
One.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:34.270
Two.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.270
Three.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.270
Four.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:37.850
Five.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.860
S-Sorry.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.040
Excuse me.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.240
You're...

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.500
So he's the Monochrome Prince 
I've heard so much about.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.730
The Monochrome Prince.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:58.980
Tsukushi!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.560
You finally came to a Hoshi Festival 
executive committee meeting.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.470
Tsukushi Monet-kun? You're...

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.840
Here.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.150
Thank you.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:12.450
Welcome to the Hoshi Festival 
executive committee.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.680
We've all been waiting for you, Tsuku Tsuku.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.140
It's Tsukushi Monet.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.270
Don't call me that.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:23.210
How cute.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:28.050
That hedgehog is Tsukushi's pet.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.070
Really?

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:34.200
Wait. I just came to say
 I can't be on the committee.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.010
What?

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.200
Oh, my.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.140
Why not, Tsukushi?

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.790
I'll be studying abroad in England.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.770
I've been invited to attend the world's 
greatest monochrome art school.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.680
I'm leaving before the Hoshi Festival.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.000
I haven't heard anything about this.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.500
Because I didn't tell you.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.840
And why do I have to tell you, Hibiki?

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.390
Are you serious?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.710
We're roommates. Don't be so cold.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:01.310
Ow!

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.820
Have you decided, Tsukushi?

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.060
Yes.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.320
Todo-sensei.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.620
I see.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:09.570
I understand.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.740
What's your problem?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.030
I thought we'd gotten to be friends, 
and now you're leaving?

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.730
Not really.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:19.570
I prefer to be alone.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:21.290
I'm disappointed, too.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:24.290
What? Oh, no.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:31.680
I just thought it would be wonderful 
to do the Art Session with you.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.510
You like my drawings that much?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.630
What? Oh, yes.

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.430
Of course you do.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.410
That unwavering confidence is great.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.690
I like it.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:45.920
Well, I'm leaving.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.440
Hey, wait.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:50.360
I understand your situation, Tsuku Tsuku.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.750
It's Tsukushi.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:56.490
Could you at least draw the cover 
for the Hoshi Festival pamphlet?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.860
Right, Georgie?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.450
I suppose.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.040
The theme is...

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:09.310
Tada! The subject of every Hoshigei 
student's adoration, the Scala Artista.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:15.640
But all our drawings look 
something like this.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.080
Yeah! I put my heart into it!

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.920
I drew mine with a bamboo shoot.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.140
Stairs are hard to draw.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.050
Are those supposed to be drawings?

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:28.470
Teika, you're one of us.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.020
What?

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.620
So if you don't draw it for us,

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:35.010
we'll have to choose one of these.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.030
Is that a threat?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:36.530
Yeah.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.000
No, thank you.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.830
What? You're so mean.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.670
Yeah, Tsukushi. Just do it.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:45.280
I don't have time for that. I can't do it.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.460
Let's go, Rin.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:48.460
Rin?

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.260
Rin, where did you go?

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.670
The hedgehog disappeared.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.470
What?

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.720
Rin! Rin!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.470
Where'd the hedgehog go?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.420
The grass looks like his spines.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.230
Yeah.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:07.200
Make sure you don't accidentally step on him.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.480
O-Okay.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.790
Rin! Rin!

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.100
Hedgehog!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.990
Hedgehog!

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:17.740
Huh?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.280
I found him!

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.280
Rin.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.080
Oh, wow.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.660
Aigasaki-senpai's flower arrangements

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.170
have the power to draw in all 
creatures of the animal kingdom.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.720
Way to go, my little flower.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.470
Y-You're exaggerating.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.900
That's your flower arrangement?

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.770
What? Oh, yes.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.420
Huh? You surprised me.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.280
You're so cute. Hello.

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.700
Hey, he really likes you.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.680
He's so cold to me.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.040
Fine.

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:06.400
What?

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:09.170
I'll draw the cover for the pamphlet.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.660
What?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.630
Seriously?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.740
Tsuku Tsuku, thank you!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.260
This is a special exception.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.180
Th-Thank you.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.060
Monet, I brought dinner.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh, thanks.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.320
Wh-What? Did you just say "thank you"?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.440
Did you, Monet?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.680
Do you have a fever?

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.450
Shut up. I don't have a fever.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.680
Rintaro, I'm going to study abroad.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.510
What? Really?

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:46.730
Yeah.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.220
You don't have any doubts?

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:50.740
What doubts?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.300
That.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.040
Your monochrome drawings are amazing.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.340
I think they are, too.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:04.970
But don't you actually want 
to make colorful drawings?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.980
Not really.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:11.270
Well, you've been used to receiving 
praise since you were little.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:12.680
Amazing!

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.270
He's a genius!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.230
When you think you've made a mistake,

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:21.030
it becomes that much scarier 
to try something else.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.710
Not really.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:25.570
It's fine, then.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:28.750
But will you be able to 
handle yourself without me?

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.180
Yeah.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.830
You sure?

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.950
You're always inside your own world.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.780
You should spend more time with other people.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.060
I'm worried about you.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:40.760
I don't need your concern.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.390
Rintaro, are you sure you're okay?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.630
What?

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.920
If you can't be on the committee,

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.240
why don't you go tell them why?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.500
Bye. Thanks for the food.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:02.460
It's okay. Rintaro is awfully squeaky, isn't he?

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:08.710
It's over. This is how it should be.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:23.550
Tsukushi, thanks for starting already.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.340
No wonder they call you 
the Monochrome Prince.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.810
You're so good at drawing.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.320
Are you making fun of me?

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:32.280
Huh? That was a compliment.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.060
I'm almost finished with the sketch.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.780
I'm sure it'll be even prettier with color.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.450
I feel like you're trying 
to pick a fight with me.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.700
We're not! Really!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.660
Aigasaki-senpai, do you know why they
 call him the Monochrome Prince?

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.080
It's because he only 
draws in black and white.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:13:00.090
Oh, I'm sorry! I...

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.960
I'm done for the day.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.340
I'll deliver it once it's done.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.340
Sure thing! Thanks.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.470
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.820
Senpai, he's gone.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.650
What should I do? I upset Tsukushi-kun.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.880
He'll be fine. He's always like that.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:21.980
Okay...

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.540
I know what Kanato-kun said,

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:40.180
but I still feel like what I said was rude.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.260
Anemone flowers.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.140
Is this where he drew this picture?

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.770
Rin-chan?

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.780
Rin. Rin.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.310
Excuse me.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:18.090
I-I'm really sorry about today.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.740
Why do you have that?

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:24.700
Oh, this? I picked it up the other day.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.510
It was blown by a strong breeze.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.140
I kept it since it was so wonderful.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:36.140
People with no artistic talent 
are poor judges of art, too.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:40.100
I can't believe you've been 
keeping such a worthless drawing.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.000
It's true that I can't 
make wonderful drawings...

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.280
But, I do know that this 
is drawing is wonderful.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.320
When I look at this drawing,

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.720
I can feel the joy you felt when 
you looked at these flowers.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.330
It makes me smile. I love it.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:01.280
You must be stupid.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:03.620
No one would like that drawing.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.840
But I like it.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:11.470
Do whatever you want.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:13.530
I'll give you the drawing tomorrow.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.740
What?

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.100
For the pamphlet.

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.930
Looks like you took care of Rin again, too.

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:22.230
I always keep my promises.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.230
Thank you.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.100
I can't believe she likes that drawing.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.120
She must be stupid. Right, Rin?

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:40.870
I'm impressed, Tsukushi-kun.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.500
Sir.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:48.020
Not many people come close to your level
 in the world of monochrome art.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.020
Thank you.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.710
By the way, have you been 
getting ready to study abroad?

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:55.520
Yes.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:58.410
I've requested that arrangements be made

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.020
so you can start next week.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.360
I understand.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.860
When I look at this drawing,

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:09.330
I can feel the joy you felt when 
you looked at these flowers.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:12.530
It makes me smile. I love it.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:22.040
Not many people come close to your 
level in the world of monochrome art.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.240
It's the Monochrome Prince.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.520
He's studying abroad?

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.040
No surprises there.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:49.570
Let's have fun today trying again 
to pass the ball ten thousand times!

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.980
Yay!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.490
Senpai, this isn't a game.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.550
Yes, sir!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:55.950
I'm looking forward to it.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:57.840
32.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.080
33.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.610
34.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:02.820
35.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:04.560
36.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.100
37.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:08.160
38.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.090
39.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.880
40.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.910
Senpai, are you okay?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.130
I'm sorry.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.540
It's fine.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:19.890
Huh? Oh.

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:24.890
It wouldn't be any fun if 
we succeeded so easily.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:28.770
Failure is the mother of success.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.280
Once you give up, it's over.

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:35.360
Yeah! Don't let it be over yet!

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.610
Yeah.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:39.910
Yeah. I'll do my best.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:40.990
I'm sure I can do it.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.500
"I'm sure I can do it"?

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.810
We'll aim for three digits next.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.760
You're raising the bar?

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.840
Teika, you're a Spartan.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:54.880
I know. Not that I dislike that.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.080
Here we go.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:57.630
Yeah!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.890
98.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:17:59.890
99.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:00.890
100.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:01.890
101.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.020
Let's keep going to four digits.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.890
Ten times what we just did?

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.400
Yikes. 104.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:10.940
I know we can do it.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.770
105.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:13.620
Yeah! 106!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:16.490
107.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:17.610
108.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:21.800
Damn it! Don't give up!

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.910
Tsukushi, get the ball!

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:28.160
But I have nothing to do with this.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:31.130
Rin?

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:34.130
One hundred and...

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.810
111.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.060
I'm not doing it again.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.070
Jeez!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.690
Thank you.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.330
I see the colors...

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.580
119.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.030
120!

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:19.460
<i>The colors drawn deep inside my heart</i>

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:27.720
<i>I was simply afraid to reach out to them</i>

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:34.230
<i>Emptiness seems boundless, 
but it's actually limited</i>

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:42.570
<i>I had honestly grown bored 
of my unchanging world</i>

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:50.410
<i>For some reason, I pretended not 
to see and tried to avoid them</i>

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:54.380
<i>But it's all because of you</i>

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:58.170
<i>Overflowing endlessly</i>

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:02.340
<i>Beyond the limits of our dreams</i>

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:07.810
<i>Shiny color sleeping in my heart</i>

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:11.430
<i>They awaken at once and begin singing</i>

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:15.530
<i>The colors I draw on the canvas</i>

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:19.690
<i>Are the ones I've always dreamed of</i>

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:23.090
<i>You've shown me a brand new world</i>

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:28.210
The inside of your heart is so shiny, 
full of brilliant colors, and fun.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.770
<i>I'll take the first step</i>

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:30.400
<i>Even if the whole world rejects me</i>

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.700
Of course.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:37.680
<i>As long as you accept me, I'll be fine</i>

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.610
Senpai, thanks for everything.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:36.240
What?

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:41.360
From now on, I'll show 
you more of my drawings.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:50.980
Amazing!

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.400
It's so shiny!

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.640
It's blindingly bright!

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.700
This year's drawing is fantastic!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.860
Hoshinomori Summer Festival

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.860
The wind has died down.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:05.240
Sir, you knew from the beginning 
that this would happen, didn't you?

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:10.370
No, though I did hope it would happen.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:15.420
But walls must be overcome 
with your own strength.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:20.170
I'm looking forward to this 
year's Hoshi Festival.

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:24.920
Tsukushi-kun.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.590
You came.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:30.630
Apparently, you guys can't 
play volleyball without me.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:33.410
We've been waiting for you, Tsuku Tsuku.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:39.060
<b>56 days until the summer festival!</b>

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.420
Come on in!

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:36.720
Your seat is over there.

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.520
There's someone else.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:43.340
He feeds me. This is my cousin Rintaro.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.870
Rin Rin, we've been waiting for you!

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.200
Tatewaki-senpai!

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.700
The entire executive committee is here now.

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:52.950
Yeah.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.950
All right!

00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.590
You're so bright.

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:29.800
You're always smiling so cheerfully.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.530
I love that about you.

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:33.550
A-All you guys.

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:36.210
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Shining Like the Sun</b>

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:38.220
"Shining Like the Sun."

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:39.310
Magic-Kyun for you!

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:39.960
Good night.
